   "source": [
    "### Step 2 — Chunking the Text\n",
    "\n",
    "Pages can be large and have too much context bundled together. Breaking them into smaller chunks helps with searching and embedding.\n",
    "\n",
    "`RecursiveCharacterTextSplitter` breaks pages into smaller overlapping pieces:\n",
    "- `chunk_size`: max characters per chunk\n",
    "- `chunk_overlap`: how much text repeats between chunks (so we don't lose context at boundaries)\n",
    "\n",
    "You'll typically get more chunks than pages. In this example: 11 pages → 76 chunks.\n"
   ]
  },
