   "id": "5dc0eda3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "I don't know.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Test grounding: unrelated questions should get \"I don't know\"\n",
    "answer, docs = ask(\"What is the capital of France?\")\n",
    "print(answer)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ecf18ecc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 7 — Now, Make It Agentic\n",
    "\n",
    "So far we just retrieve and generate. But different questions need different handling:\n",
    "- Broad questions (\"What is this paper about?\") need a summary of the whole document\n",
    "- Specific questions (\"What is self-attention?\") need targeted retrieval\n",
    "- Unrelated questions should be rejected instead of making stuff up\n",
    "\n",
    "LangGraph lets us build a decision tree (state machine) to handle these cases. It has three key pieces:\n",
    "- **State**: a dictionary that flows through the pipeline, accumulating data\n",
    "- **Nodes**: functions that process the state\n",
    "- **Edges**: connections between nodes (fixed or conditional)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bc4768ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 8 — Define the State\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 31,
   "id": "5582ae89",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from typing import TypedDict, List\n",
    "from langchain_core.documents import Document\n",
    "\n",
    "class AgentState(TypedDict):\n",
    "    question: str          # The user's question\n",
    "    search_query: str       # Rewritten version (removes pronouns like \"it\")\n",
    "    chat_history: str        # Previous conversation for context\n",
    "    question_type: str        # \"broad\" or \"specific\"\n",
    "    docs: List[Document]        # Retrieved chunks\n",
    "    is_relevant: bool             # Whether docs answer the question\n",
    "    answer: str                     # Final answer\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bc4768ff",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 9 — Build the Nodes\n",
    "\n",
    "Each node is a small function that does one job. Read them in order — this is how data flows through the graph.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1bdb3acb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Classify Node** — Does the question ask about the whole paper or just one thing?\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 32,
   "id": "7f42f623",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "classify_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"\"\"\n",
    "Given the recent conversation, classify the CURRENT question into ONE category:\n",
    "\n",
    "- \"broad\": asking about the ENTIRE document — its overall topic, main contributions, or summary\n",
    "  Examples: \"What is this paper about?\", \"Summarize this document\"\n",
    "\n",
    "- \"specific\": asking about ONE particular concept, term, or fact\n",
    "  Examples: \"What is self-attention?\", \"Why is it useful?\"\n",
    "\n",
    "Recent conversation:\n",
    "{chat_history}\n",
    "\n",
    "Current question: {question}\n",
    "\n",
    "Reply with ONLY one word: \"broad\" or \"specific\".\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def classify_question_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    chain = classify_prompt | llm\n",
    "    response = chain.invoke({\n",
    "        \"question\": state[\"question\"],\n",
    "        \"chat_history\": state.get(\"chat_history\", \"\"),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    verdict = str(response.content).strip().lower()\n",
    "    state[\"question_type\"] = \"broad\" if \"broad\" in verdict else \"specific\"\n",
    "    return state\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "1bdb3acb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Retrieve Node** — For specific questions. First rewrites the query to remove pronouns, then searches.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 33,
   "id": "35e9171e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rewrite_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"\"\"\n",
    "Rewrite the follow-up question into a standalone version using the conversation.\n",
    "If it's already standalone, just repeat it.\n",
    "\n",
    "Recent conversation:\n",
    "{chat_history}\n",
    "\n",
    "Follow-up question: {question}\n",
    "\n",
    "Standalone question:\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def retrieve_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    chat_history = state.get(\"chat_history\", \"\")\n",
    "    if chat_history.strip():\n",
    "        chain = rewrite_prompt | llm\n",
    "        response = chain.invoke({\"chat_history\": chat_history, \"question\": state[\"question\"]})\n",
    "        search_query = str(response.content).strip()\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        search_query = state[\"question\"]\n",
    "\n",
    "    state[\"search_query\"] = search_query\n",
    "    docs = loaded_vectorstore.similarity_search(search_query, k=5)\n",
    "    state[\"docs\"] = docs\n",
    "    return state\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9f719ea7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Relevance Check Node** — Make sure the retrieved chunks actually answer the question. FAISS always returns something, but we want to catch when it's not relevant.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 34,
   "id": "78f45d5e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "relevance_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"\"\"\n",
    "Does the context contain information that could answer this question?\n",
    "Reply with ONLY one word: \"yes\" or \"no\".\n",
    "\n",
    "Context:\n",
    "{context}\n",
    "\n",
    "Question: {question}\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def check_relevance_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    context = \"\\n\\n\".join(doc.page_content for doc in state[\"docs\"])\n",
    "    chain = relevance_prompt | llm\n",
    "    response = chain.invoke({\n",
    "        \"context\": context,\n",
    "        \"question\": state.get(\"search_query\", state[\"question\"]),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    verdict = str(response.content).strip().lower()\n",
    "    state[\"is_relevant\"] = \"yes\" in verdict\n",
    "    return state\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "3dc8a77f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Generate Node** — Answer using retrieved context. **No Context Node** — If nothing relevant was found, say so.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 35,
   "id": "3d3b66c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "rag_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"\"\"\n",
    "You are a research assistant. Answer the question using ONLY the context below.\n",
    "If the answer isn't in the context, say you don't know.\n",
    "\n",
    "Recent conversation:\n",
    "{chat_history}\n",
    "\n",
    "Context:\n",
    "{context}\n",
    "\n",
    "Question: {question}\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def generate_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    context = \"\\n\\n\".join(doc.page_content for doc in state[\"docs\"])\n",
    "    chain = rag_prompt | llm\n",
    "    response = chain.invoke({\n",
    "        \"context\": context,\n",
    "        \"question\": state[\"question\"],\n",
    "        \"chat_history\": state.get(\"chat_history\", \"\"),\n",
    "    })\n",
    "    state[\"answer\"] = str(response.content)\n",
    "    return state\n",
    "\n",
    "def no_context_response_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    state[\"answer\"] = \"I couldn't find relevant information in the document to answer that question.\"\n",
    "    state[\"docs\"] = []  # Clear these — they weren't useful\n",
    "    return state\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b7176afe",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "**Summarize Node** — For broad questions. Takes the first 40 chunks and summarizes them (to stay under rate limits).\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 36,
   "id": "cab9e87d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "summarize_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"\"\"\n",
    "Summarize the document below to answer this question:\n",
    "\n",
    "Document:\n",
    "{full_text}\n",
    "\n",
    "Question: {question}\n",
    "\"\"\")\n",
    "\n",
    "def summarize_node(state: AgentState) -> AgentState:\n",
    "    max_chunks = 40\n",
    "    limited_chunks = chunks[:max_chunks]\n",
    "    full_text = \"\\n\\n\".join(chunk.page_content for chunk in limited_chunks)\n",
    "    chain = summarize_prompt | llm\n",
    "    response = chain.invoke({\"full_text\": full_text, \"question\": state[\"question\"]})\n",
    "    state[\"answer\"] = str(response.content)\n",
    "    return state\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "864371a3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 10 — Routing Functions\n",
    "\n",
    "These decide which node runs next based on the state.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 37,
   "id": "4ee9ed45",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def route_after_classify(state: AgentState) -> str:\n",
    "    return \"summarize\" if state[\"question_type\"] == \"broad\" else \"retrieve\"\n",
    "\n",
    "def route_after_relevance_check(state: AgentState) -> str:\n",
    "    return \"generate\" if state[\"is_relevant\"] else \"no_context_response\"\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0e3f7c82",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Step 11 — Wire It All Together\n",
    "\n",
    "Here's the flow:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "classify ──broad──► summarize ──► END\n",
    "   │\n",
    "   └──specific──► retrieve ──► check_relevance ──relevant──► generate ──► END\n",
    "                                      │\n",
    "                                      └──not relevant──► no_context_response ──► END\n",
    "```\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "ef883c8a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Graph compiled successfully.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from langgraph.graph import StateGraph, END\n",
    "\n",
    "graph = StateGraph(AgentState)\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"classify\", classify_question_node)\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"summarize\", summarize_node)\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"retrieve\", retrieve_node)\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"check_relevance\", check_relevance_node)\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"no_context_response\", no_context_response_node)\n",
    "graph.add_node(\"generate\", generate_node)\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.set_entry_point(\"classify\")\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.add_conditional_edges(\n",
    "    \"classify\",\n",
    "    route_after_classify,\n",
    "    {\"summarize\": \"summarize\", \"retrieve\": \"retrieve\"},\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"retrieve\", \"check_relevance\")\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.add_conditional_edges(\n",
    "    \"check_relevance\",\n",
    "    route_after_relevance_check,\n",
    "    {\"generate\": \"generate\", \"no_context_response\": \"no_context_response\"},\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"generate\", END)\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"no_context_response\", END)\n",
    "graph.add_edge(\"summarize\", END)\n",
    "\n",
    "app = graph.compile()\n",
    "print(\"Graph compiled successfully.\")\n"
   ]
  },
  {
